{% extends "layouts/app.njk" %}
{% from "govuk/components/summary-list/macro.njk" import govukSummaryList %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}

{#
  Check your direction — the attestation step, and the only page in this repo that has one.

  **The answers are in the page twice, and both copies are needed.** The summary list is what the judge reads
  back; the three hidden fields are what the confirm carries to api. Nothing is stored between the form and this
  page — no draft, client or server (decision 7) — so the request is the only place the direction exists until
  it is recorded.

  **Change is a submit, not a link.** A `GET` back to the form would arrive with nothing in it, because there is
  no stored answer to re-read; re-posting the same three fields is what makes the form come back filled in. It
  is styled as a secondary button so it does not compete with the confirm.

  **The declaration sits above the submit rather than in a tick box.** Pressing the button *is* the attestation,
  which is the Design System's check-answers pattern; the sentence beside it says so, and the one below says
  what happens afterwards.
#}
{% block content %}
<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    {% if reference %}
      <span class="govuk-caption-l">{{ reference }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">{{ checkHeading }}</h1>

    {#
      No change links on the rows, for the reason the docblock gives: every way back to the form has to carry the
      answers with it, and a summary-list action is a link. The one Change control is the button below, so there
      is one way back rather than three that behave differently.
    #}
    {{ govukSummaryList({
      rows: [
        { key: { text: decisionLabel }, value: { text: answers.decision } },
        { key: { text: gazetteLabel }, value: { text: yes if answers.changesToStandardPublication else no } },
        { key: { text: directionsSummaryLabel }, value: { text: answers.directionsText if answers.directionsText else noneGiven } }
      ]
    }) }}

    <form method="post" action="{{ directionHref }}" novalidate>
      <input type="hidden" name="decision" value="{{ values.decision }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="directionsText" value="{{ values.directionsText }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="changesToStandardPublication" value="{{ values.changesToStandardPublication }}">

      <p class="govuk-body">{{ declaration }}</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">{{ afterwards }}</p>

      {#
        `preventDoubleClick` on the confirm only. It is the one submit here that records something, and a second
        one cannot record it again: api 409s it, so the response the judge is left looking at is
        "not waiting for a direction from you" rather than the success banner beside the direction they just
        recorded. Both sentences are true of a judge who has already directed it, which is why the server side
        needs no change — this stops the refusal being shown for a direction that went in. Change re-renders and
        is safe to press twice.
      #}
      <div class="govuk-button-group">
        {{ govukButton({ text: confirm, name: "action", value: "confirm", preventDoubleClick: true }) }}
        {{ govukButton({ text: change, name: "action", value: "change", classes: "govuk-button--secondary" }) }}
        <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ referralHref }}">{{ cancel }}</a>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
